WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.171
An intent is when you sign only what you need:

2
00:00:03.171 --> 00:00:05.809
sell ether no cheaper than a certain price.

3
00:00:05.809 --> 00:00:07.955
How to do it is decided by solvers.

4
00:00:07.955 --> 00:00:09.918
They compete in a Dutch auction,

5
00:00:09.918 --> 00:00:13.169
where the price gradually worsens down to your bound.

6
00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:15.438
The strongest has no reason to hurry:

7
00:00:15.438 --> 00:00:19.118
it takes the trade just when the second is about to step in.

8
00:00:20.118 --> 00:00:22.273
So the price is set by competition:

9
00:00:22.273 --> 00:00:27.320
the more solvers and the lower their costs, the closer the price is to the market.

10
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.460
Without rivals, the trade goes at your lower bound.

11
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:34.091
Set it thoughtfully, and do not give an intent a long life:

12
00:00:34.091 --> 00:00:36.246
it is a free option for the solver.
